      "a": "-\nGiven that,\n$A=\\left\\{ 2,4,8,12 \\right\\},B=\\left\\{ 1,2,3,4 \\right\\},C=\\left\\{ 4,8,12,14 \\right\\},D=\\left\\{ 3,1,4,2 \\right\\}$\n$E=\\left\\{ -1,1 \\right\\},F=\\left\\{ 0,a \\right\\},G=\\left\\{ 1,-1 \\right\\},H=\\left\\{ 0,1 \\right\\}$\nTo select equal sets from the given set\nTwo sets A and B are said to be equal if they have exactly the same elements and we write A = B\nWe can observe from the sets that,\n$8\\in A,8\\notin B,8\\notin D,8\\notin E,8\\notin F,8\\notin G,8\\notin H$\nAnd thus\n$A\\ne B,A\\ne D,A\\ne E,A\\ne F,A\\ne G,A\\ne H$\nBut $8\\in C$\nAnd checking other elements,\n$2\\in A,2\\notin C$\nSo $A\\ne C$\n$3\\in B,3\\notin C,3\\notin E,3\\notin F,3\\notin G,3\\notin H$\nAnd thus,\n$B\\ne C,B\\ne E,B\\ne F,B\\ne G,B\\ne H$\n$12\\in C,12\\notin D,12\\notin E,12\\notin F,12\\notin G,12\\notin H$\nAnd thus\n$C\\ne D,C\\ne E,C\\ne F,C\\ne G,C\\ne H$\n$4\\in D,4\\notin E,4\\notin F,4\\notin G,4\\notin H$\nAnd thus,\n$D\\ne E,D\\ne F,D\\ne G,D\\ne H$\nSimilarly $E\\ne F,E\\ne G,E\\ne H$\n$F\\ne G,F\\ne H$\n$G\\ne H$\nWe know that the order of the elements I listed are insignificant.\nSo $B=D,E=G$\n$\\therefore $He equal sets are $B=D$ and $E=G$\nExercise 1.3"
